      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`embed_mm_inputs` clamps caller-owned IDs in place, destroying multimodal placeholders and potentially modifying a packed batch through a tensor view.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Clamp a temporary tensor for the text-embedding lookup, matching the split-batch path.\n- Test owned tensors and views across repeated calls: IDs/backing storage stay unchanged, and image/text embedding rows remain correct.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nAll **19 CPU cases** in `test_mm_embed_scatter.py` pass. Both new ownership cases fail on unpatched upstream; its 17 existing scatter cases still pass.\n\nGPU/serving validation has not been run. Upstream CI requires the maintainer `run-ci` label.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot benchmarked; no performance claim or kernel changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Project isort/ruff checks pass.\n- [x] Parameterized regression added to the existing CPU module.\n- [x] No documentation change needed.\n- [ ] GPU/serving validation.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38942794837](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38942794837)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38942794760](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38942794760)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38942794520](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38942794520)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
